Z||000000||85ZainoGT||09-23-2001||12:32 PM||||I was out driving last night, and after about an hour, it all the sudden got hard to shift into first, from first to second, and second to third... anyone have any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||JayUSA77||09-23-2001||01:17 PM||||the only thing it can be is the slave cylinder,or there is air in the system. Go get a friend and see if you can get all the air out. If that doesnt work its your slave cylinder.  In very rare occations the clutch master cylinder goes out.  When you put down your clutch do you feel less resistance??? try to pump your clutch a couple quick times before you shift to other gears that should help. But watch out because nomatter what you do eventually it will go completley out and when i say that i mean it, i was stuck in first for 2 miles all the way home. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
